theory.intro:
The cosine rule extends Pythagoras' theorem to any triangle. When you know **two sides and the angle between them** (the included angle), it finds the third side — the one opposite that angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.5,2.9);
\draw (V)--(B) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\draw (V)--(A) node[midway,above left] {$b$};
\draw (B)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$c$};
\pic[draw,"$C$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=B--V--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

facts:
If the included angle is obtuse, $\cos C$ is **negative**, so $-2ab\cos C$ adds on and the third side comes out longer.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-1.38,2.96);
\draw (V)--(B) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\draw (V)--(A) node[midway,left] {$b$};
\draw (B)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$c$};
\pic[draw,"$C$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=B--V--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.864,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.113,3.973);
\draw (V)--(A) node[midway,below] {$7$};
\draw (V)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$11$};
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$x$};
\pic[draw,"$62^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.35] {angle=A--V--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the length $x$, correct to $2$ decimal places.

foundation.solution_text:
$c^{2}=a^{2}+b^{2}-2ab\cos C$
$x^{2}=7^{2}+11^{2}-2(7)(11)\cos 62^{\circ}$
$x=\sqrt{7^{2}+11^{2}-2(7)(11)\cos 62^{\circ}}$
$\approx 9.88$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (2.864,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.113,3.973);
\draw (V)--(A) node[midway,below] {$7$};
\draw (V)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$11$};
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$9.88$};
\pic[draw,"$62^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=1.35] {angle=A--V--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

